From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erfan Abdi <erfangplus@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linker: cfg.d lines that map only the app namespace's lookups

apklayer patch (docs/PATCHES.md). volk (Godot 4, and other engines) opens "libvulkan.so.1" before "libvulkan.so"; on a device
the first fails, here it found the host's glibc loader, which has no VK_KHR_android_surface, so Godot's Vulkan context failed.
apklayer's own Vulkan driver (vulkan.apklayer.so, a system library) opens the host loader by that same name. A cfg.d line
"app:<name> <target>" now maps <name> only when the app namespace asks for it (an app's library or its dlopen), so apps get
Android's loader under both names and the driver keeps the host's.

--- a/linker/linker.c
+++ b/linker/linker.c
@@ -1646,7 +1646,11 @@
 		name += prefix64_len;

 	for(int i = 0; i < lib_override_map.len; i++) {
-		if(!strcmp(lib_override_map.overrides[i].from, name)) {
+		/* apklayer patch: an "app:<name>" line maps only what the app namespace asks for (the app's own libraries and their dlopens) */
+		const char *from = lib_override_map.overrides[i].from;
+		if (!strncmp(from, "app:", 4) && !(from += 4, app))
+			continue;
+		if(!strcmp(from, name)) {
 			name = lib_override_map.overrides[i].to;
 			break;
 		}
